WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.960
Friday edition of Tesla Short's Time, Episode 544 for July 17th, 2026.

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:08.800
I'm Patrick, coming to you from Vancouver.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:11.900
Here's what's wrapping up the week in Tesla Land.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:15.760
Tesla opens its first public mega-charger in California,

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:19.700
unlocking 1.2 megawatts speeds for semi-fleets.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:23.580
The station in Bloomington, about an hour east of Los Angeles,

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:28.340
features six stalls each rated for 1.2 megawatts peak power.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:32.260
It is open to all Tesla semi-customers and represents

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:35.400
the first public high-power charging option for the truck.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:39.160
This extends the charging network beyond fleet depots

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:42.460
and supports longer roads for early semi-operators.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:47.000
The development ties directly into the ongoing semi-production ramp

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:51.020
at Giga Texas, where real-world range and charging logistics

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:52.720
remain key open questions.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.860
Listeners should watch for utilization data once more units are on the road.

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:01.280
Yesterday we covered the latest semi-fleet activity,

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:05.300
and this public site moves the commercial operations story forward

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:08.600
by testing high-power economics outside depots.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:12.700
The semi will headline two fleet-focused events this month.

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:16.160
The truck is scheduled to appear at a pair of industry gatherings

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:18.280
aimed at commercial fleet operators.

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:22.420
These appearances follow the opening of the public mega-charger.

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:25.600
Fleet economics and real-world uptime remain

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:28.420
the primary metrics fleet managers are evaluating.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:32.540
Production volume at Giga Texas continues to set the pace

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:33.900
for wider availability.

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:37.480
The events continue the truck's gradual introduction

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:40.080
to potential buyers beyond early adopters.

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:43.680
Now shifting from charging infrastructure to the vehicle

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:44.900
that will use it most.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:49.760
Tesla launched Robotaxi Service in Miami with a limited footprint.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:53.680
The initial deployment covers a small geographic zone

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:56.260
due to regulatory and operational limits.

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:59.120
Early users are testing within boundaries,

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:02.300
and expansion is tied to safety data and approvals.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:06.340
This connects to the CyberCab program we discussed yesterday,

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:10.560
where unsupervised regulatory approval and production timeline

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.580
remain the primary gating items.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:16.140
The small service area shows how current constraints

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:20.080
shape the early rollout before wider unsupervised operation.

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:22.780
Attentive listeners will want to track

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:24.920
what additional approvals come next.

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:27.160
From current autonomy progress,

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:31.060
we turn to the broader financial picture investors will hear next.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:35.420
Tesla scheduled its Q2 earnings call for July 22.

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:40.600
The webcast is set for 5.30 pm ET with live Q&amp;A.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:45.240
Focus is expected on Robotaxi, Optimus, and Energy Storage.

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:48.240
The call follows the recent delivery beat

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:50.380
and the three pronged growth strategy.

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:55.560
Investors will listen for updates on how these programs fit into capital plans.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:03:01.040
From Tesla's own capital plans, we move to an external energy move by its leader.

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:07.640
Musk acquired an energy firm valued at approximately $1 billion for AI compute needs.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:14.140
Federal Trade Commission filing show the purchase of new APR energy via a holding company.

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:19.920
The acquired assets add generation capacity whose integration with Tesla energy remains

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:26.000
undisclosed. The move brings additional power resources that could support large-scale compute

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:32.760
loads. From large-scale energy assets, we look at how Tesla is faring in one key emerging market.

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:40.260
Tesla posted muted first-year results in India. Fewer than 500 vehicles were registered while German

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:46.460
luxury brands outsold it significantly. High import duties and the lack of local production keep

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:51.980
prices uncompetitive. The company has not announced plans for an assembly facility there.

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:58.700
Success will depend on future policy changes or lower-cost models. From sales headwinds abroad,

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:06.300
we turn to a straightforward regulatory fix at home. NHTSA ordered a headlight fix on older Tesla

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:11.540
models. The recall targets specific earlier builds to meet federal lighting standards.

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:17.600
Free repairs will be available at service centers. No production line changes are required,

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:23.660
indicating the issue is limited to vehicles already on the road. Owners will receive notices for

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:30.560
the work. From hardware recalls, we move to software-driven performance quirks. The new model Y

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:37.020
Performance posted faster zero to 60 times without launch mode engaged. Testing showed quicker

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:42.600
acceleration when the mode is not used. The result suggests power train mapping or traction

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:49.360
behavior differs under the preset parameters. Owners seeking quickest times may need to adjust their

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:54.680
routine. The finding highlights how software calibration affects expected performance.

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:59.520
From vehicle dynamics, we turn to smaller product and market updates.

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:06.540
Bioweapon defense mode is now standard on more trims. The HEPA filtration system is included at

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:12.960
no extra cost on select model Y and Cybertruck variants. It was previously optional on some

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:18.760
configurations. The change differentiates premium hardware offerings through included features.

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:25.460
It improves cabin air quality in polluted or wildfire prone regions. From in-car features,

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:31.500
we move to new retail and consumer items. Tesla entered Uruguay with the Model 3

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:37.780
and Model Y. Direct sales began using existing right-hand drive and left-hand drive variants.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:44.520
No volume targets or pricing details were released. The move adds another South American market

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:50.700
to the Direct Sales footprint. It follows the pattern of incremental country by country expansions.

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:57.560
From new markets, we turn to non-vehicle Tesla branded products. Tesla launched a magnesium

00:05:57.560 --> 00:06:06.220
balance bike for kids. The $225 model is for ages 2-5 with 5 height settings and a 66.1 pound

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:13.500
weight limit. Minimum leg length is listed at 13.7 inches. The product carries the Tesla word

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:19.540
mark and is sold directly through the company store. It extends the line of branded consumer goods

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:25.920
beyond a peril. Tesla's low-cost vehicle program continues to target aggressive cost reductions

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:31.840
while maintaining core vehicle capabilities. Specific engineering and manufacturing approaches

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:37.860
remain under development. No customer delivery window has been confirmed. The effort is separate

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:44.080
from the current Model 3 and Model Y lines. The program aims at a distinct vehicle line focused

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:50.100
on lower price points. Development work continues without overlap to existing production vehicles.

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:54.740
From retail products, we turn to the week's deeper infrastructure discussion.

00:06:55.460 --> 00:07:01.320
Owners report that FSD can be toggled mid-drive to correct routing without stopping the vehicle.

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:06.140
The workaround addresses cases where the system selects an undesired route.

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:12.520
Drivers are actively managing the supervised system in real time while navigation logic improves.

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:17.580
The behavior shows a practical response to current supervised limitations.

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:24.440
Exping announced plans to begin mass production of its own humanoid robots by late 2026.

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:31.020
The timeline positions the Chinese automaker as an early competitor in the physical AI hardware

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:37.160
space. No details on target applications or unit economics were released with the announcement.

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:42.480
The move adds another entrant to the race alongside Tesla's Optimus program,

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:49.460
or volume production remains targeted for 2027 and beyond. An X-Pung SUV was spotted

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:56.560
charging at a Tesla supercharger in Australia during testing. The siding suggests ongoing interoperability

00:07:56.560 --> 00:08:02.560
work or simple convenience for the development team. It highlights how non-Tesla vehicles are

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:08.340
increasingly accessing the network. No official partnership details were shared. There is a

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:14.400
challenge worth discussing in Tesla's India operations. The company registered fewer than 500

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:21.080
vehicles in its first full year. Ludgery German brands posted significantly higher volumes during

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:27.100
the same period. Import duties and the absence of local manufacturing continue to limit price

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:33.440
competitiveness. The company has not signaled plans for an Indian assembly site. Successful

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:38.920
depend on whether policy changes or a future lower cost model can improve affordability.

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:44.780
Charging infrastructure has traditionally been sized to the daily energy needs of passenger cars.

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:51.860
Tesla's decision to place a 1.2 MW public megacharger therefore sits outside that frame.

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:59.020
The stall rating is driven by the energy density and duty cycle of the semi, not by sedan or SUV

00:08:59.020 --> 00:09:04.600
patterns. This reverses the usual sequence in which light duty vehicles set the specification

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:11.840
and commercial trucks follow. A 1.2 MW connection demands upstream electrical infrastructure that

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:18.160
most retail sites never contemplated. For Tesla energy, the implication is straightforward because

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:23.800
mega-packed deployments can now be cited to serve both grid services and vehicle charging without

00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:29.700
separate interconnection studies. The open question is whether the same sites can maintain high

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:37.080
utilization once semi-volumes rise. Before we go, keep an eye on how the Miami Robotaxi service area

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:42.860
evolves with the next round of regulatory feedback. That covers it for today's Tesla developments.

